    "title": "Names released of people killed in deadly Minong wrong-way crash | Local & State News | fox21online.com",
    "text": "MINOG, Wis. (KQDS-TV) - A two-vehicle crash happened at mile post 191 northbound on US 53 in Douglas County. It was on Wednesday November 4, 2026 just before 6pm.\nThe Wisconsin State Patrol said both vehicles were in the northbound lanes when they collided. The drivers were the only occupants of both vehicles.\nThe initial release from the Wisconsin State Patrol did not say which vehicle was in the incorrect lane.\nOne person was James Paske, 80, from Minong.\nThe other person was Nicholas Groszbach, 37, of Hibbing.\nA GoFundMe page has been set-up for Groszbach's family.\nThe GoFundMe says Groszbach was driving home from work when the crash happened. He left behind his wife, Pia, and their three young children.\nHe was the family’s main source of income. The initial goal of the fundraiser was $26,000. It reached more than $16,000 in just eight hours.",
    "summary": "MINOG, Wis. (KQDS-TV) - A two-vehicle crash happened at mile post 191 northbound on US 53 in Douglas County. The Wisconsin State Patrol said both vehicles were in the northbound lanes when they collided. The initial release from the Wisconsin State Patrol did not say which vehicle was in the incorrect lane. A GoFundMe page has been set-up for Groszbach's family. The GoFundMe says Groszbach was driving home from work when the crash happened.",
